  "methodology": [
    "Only exact controller state paths, native journals, crew.json and parsed loop.log event fields were read. No secrets, raw logs, process arguments, or sequence strings were emitted.",
    "Fresh/repeat counts sum completed worker result counters, cross-checked against repeat=1 journal observations and continuation native_attempted_hashes.",
    "Gate reasons use native observation journals, which distinguish completed Aggrescan cap failures from tool failures. Raw worker aggrescan_unavailable_or_failed rejection labels are not interpreted as execution errors.",
    "Counts of native_passed_before_novelty across attempts are not unique counts because confirmation carry can reclassify a previously evaluated candidate. Distinct post-novelty hashes and final continuation sets provide unique downstream counts.",
    "Consumer commit events are associated with the most recent epoch event in the serial loop log; plan/done totals and individual uid rc values agree. Registration count is the final chain-refreshed crew snapshot, not a new independent live-chain query.",
    "The report proves successful submit-host commit receipts. It does not claim validator acceptance, ranking, or reward."
