  "findings": [
    "Epoch25965 low UID count was sequence availability: pool3, registered13, planned3, committed3, failed0. Epoch25966 used full registered fleet: pool18, planned13, committed13, failed0.",
    "No publisher correction is warranted: final native hash sets equal published pools in both epochs and contain no invalidated hashes. Final epoch25966 upgrade refusal preserved the same18 sequences.",
    "Native execution errors were one timeout per completed epoch; the bulk loss was true native gate rejection. The gate mix differed between epoch-bound runs. Requirement changes are listed separately; the counts alone do not establish causality or justify relaxing gates.",
    "End-of-epoch idle is deliberate admission conservatism: native continuation requires695seconds; sequence continuation755seconds with configured130second native window,10cleanup,300novelty,15setup,90score,150publish. Final remaining time was below the corresponding floor.",
    "A small avoidable orchestration repeat occurred in attempt2 of both epochs: completed native checkpoints rejected by novelty were requeued, performed zero new measurements, and repeated novelty. Costs52.6seconds in25965 and26.4seconds in25966 plus inter-attempt polling.",
    "Additional potential throughput work: native work is paused during GPU scoring, and worker batch barriers leave most CPU slots idle during 1-to6-candidate confirmation batches. These are design opportunities requiring separate bounded changes and tests, not evidence of stuck workers."
